# Logging — the keys stored in secrets.sops.json, one value each (`sopsgen
# apply` fills generated ones, `sopsedit` the rest). Values built from other
# secrets live in env.nix. Key set must match secrets.sops.json and
# tests/fixtures/stacks/logging.sops.json.
# Only Grafana has secrets — VictoriaLogs and Alloy authenticate to nothing and
# must not acquire an env_file.

# Grafana
# READ ONCE, when grafana.db is created. Changing them later does nothing
# visible; rotate with `docker exec -it grafana grafana-cli admin
# reset-admin-password '<new>'` and mirror it back here. This is the second
# login underneath forward auth, beside "Sign in with Authentik", on purpose:
# a local admin that still works when Authentik is down is the property worth
# keeping. The OAuth client secret is not stored here — env.nix builds it
# from the shared file.
# openssl rand -base64 30
GF_SECURITY_ADMIN_USER=changeme_grafana_admin_username
GF_SECURITY_ADMIN_PASSWORD=changeme_long_random_password
